{"reference":"Psalms 50","book":"Psalms","chapter":50,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Psalm Headings","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The received headings of the Psalms associate psalms with figures and groups such as David, Asaph, the sons of Korah, Solomon, Moses, Heman, and Ethan. They may also preserve labels for genre, performance, tunes, instruments, or narrated settings. These headings can guide interpretation, while also raising questions about how their associations and labels should be understood.","verse_refs":["Psalms 50:1"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_050_78b31998d8c8403a49b0d59b"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}